Z||000000||FieroSoul||12-30-2001||09:09 AM||||  I started my 84 to go to work the other day and the gas gage pegged far right.  I had about half a tank in it.  Anyone have any suggestions on where to start looking?  Is it most likely the gage or the sending unit.  BTW the Temp sensor is operating fine in case they share the same circuitry.||||reg||9
Z||000001||GTDude||12-30-2001||09:51 AM||||most likely cause is a loose connection at the tank or in the dash.  Smack the dash a few times....not too hard.  If it starts working it's just a loose connection in the dash.  Easily fixed.  If this doesn't workm, I would ground the wire going to the tank....it'd s pink wire in the 4 wire connector going to the tank.  Unplug it first.  If it goes to empty then.....you either have a bad fuel sender or a bad ground  at the tank.  Hope this helps.<P>Phil Pettus<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSCF0003a_7.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroSoul||12-30-2001||10:54 AM||||  Thanks, I have some time to tinker with it today and I will check that.  Already tried the smack with no luck.  May try some good fuel system to see if corrosion is a possibility. I will let you know. The joys of owning and driving a classic...<BR>  I wish you were close by, I would love to take a look at the Gt you want ot sell...||||reg||14
